fail[3]: 0 and 1 touch: `[[0, 1]]`.
fail[4]: 9 fills the gap between 8 and 10 and joins them.
fail[5]: 2 joins [1, 1] and [3, 3] into [1, 3].
fail[6]: 3,300 values that end up as one interval. Checking a list of all the values for repeats, or building the intervals from all the values, takes far too long.
